Summary: Rosetta 2: report success when setting debug registers instead of failing
Category: cpu
Kind: workaround
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.3.0
  CW-Hacks: 22131
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz
  Note: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 22131 (dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c), verbatim
    Source: (sources/wine/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c)
Upstream: partly: WineHQ already fakes zeroed debug registers in wineserver (is_rosetta() in server/mach.c, 10.0 included); this ntdll half isn't upstream
Why: Rosetta 2 cannot set or read x86 debug registers; report success from NtSetContextThread / the wow64 set-context path instead of failing, so anti-debug/DRM checks and debuggers don't abort.
Programs: Big Fish games (Armadillo DRM): setting debug registers fails
 under Rosetta (Armadillo's parent relies on the faked success)
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: ntdll.so: "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking success"; wineserver: "%04x: thread_get_state failed on Apple Silicon - faking zero debug registers"
Port: to 11.21: ntdll half is CX 26.3.0's CW HACK 22131, identical to 25.1.1's. The 10.0 patch's wineserver half (CX HACK 21217, fake zero debug registers in server/mach.c get_thread_context) is dropped: WineHQ 11.21 already has it as is_rosetta() in server/mach.c (get_thread_context returns zeroed debug registers, set_thread_context returns STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL, which this hack turns into success), and CX 26.3.0 no longer carries 21217.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 7bff70b..adc9260 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -1003,7 +1003,11 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetContextThread( HANDLE handle, const CONTEXT *context )
         ret = set_thread_context( handle, context, &self, IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64 );
 #ifdef __APPLE__
         if ((flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) && (ret == STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL))
-            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta\n" );
+        {
+            /* CW HACK 22131 */
+            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking success\n" );
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
 #endif
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
@@ -1234,6 +1238,14 @@ NTSTATUS set_thread_wow64_context( HANDLE handle, const void *ctx, ULONG size )
     if (!self)
     {
         NTSTATUS ret = set_thread_context( handle, context, &self, IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_I386 );
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+        if ((flags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS) && (ret == STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL))
+        {
+            /* CW HACK 22131 */
+            WARN_(seh)( "Setting debug registers is not supported under Rosetta, faking success\n" );
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+        }
+#endif
         if (ret || !self) return ret;
         if (flags & CONTEXT_I386_DEBUG_REGISTERS)
         {
